# Scattering table with a tabulated aerosol phase function (test data, not a fitted model).
# Main rows: scattering_exponential.dat, rows at 354 and 355 nm for the altitude nodes
# 0.1 0.5 1 2 4 8 15 30 60 km (copied, values unchanged). ssa = 0.9, g = 0.65.
# Phase rows: Henyey-Greenstein p(theta) for g = 0.65 at 0..180 deg, step 1 deg, the same
# function for every (wavelength, altitude) pair, divided by the trapezoid-rule norm
# 2 pi int p d(cos theta) (1.000294 before division), printed with 8 significant digits.
# Generated by a short python3 script (stdlib only): p = (1-g^2)/(4 pi (1+g^2-2g cos)^1.5).
# Used by test_scattering.cpp to compare the tabulated phase with the analytic HG result.
